# Line endings.
#
# This repo shipped with three files in CRLF (models/create-entities.ts,
# models/read-entities.ts, ui/modals/travel-place-picker-modal.ts) and every
# other text file in LF. That mix stays invisible until it isn't: a two-line
# edit to one of the three rewrote all 142 lines of the file, and the change
# that mattered sat buried in a diff nobody would read. LF everywhere,
# decided here once, rather than by whichever editor last saved the file.
#
# .prettierrc keeps endOfLine: "auto", which preserves whatever a file
# already has. That stays the right setting now that this file exists: git
# owns the decision and prettier does not argue with it.
#
# An existing checkout needs one pass to catch up:
#   git add --renormalize .
# Worth its own commit, so the whitespace churn never rides along with a
# real change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated, tracked, and never read by a human. Collapsed in diffs and kept
# out of the repo's language statistics.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated=true

# Binary, marked explicitly rather than left to git's content heuristic: a
# PDF or PNG that gets line-ending conversion applied to it is a corrupt PDF
# or PNG.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
